WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.919 line:85%
[MUSIC]

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.239 line:85%
Hello and welcome.

00:00:22.559 --> 00:00:25.160 line:83%
I'm Andrei Panko and
I will be demonstrating to

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:27.519 line:83%
you how to create
troubles and how to solve them

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:30.280 line:83%
when you're dealing
with Shopify integrations.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.240 line:85%
It's an overview session.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.200 line:83%
It includes also
functionality which existed

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.799 line:83%
before, but now we have
even more troubleshooting things

00:00:40.159 --> 00:00:42.640 line:83%
which is actually very
difficult to demonstrate because

00:00:42.679 --> 00:00:45.280 line:83%
we also dramatically
increased stability of the product.

00:00:45.679 --> 00:00:50.079 line:83%
But I work hard to
actually create some issues.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.880 position:75% line:83%
So we will take a look how
troubleshoot things using logging functionality.

00:00:55.679 --> 00:01:00.320 position:56% line:83%
What is Shopify API
versioning and what impact it has or

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:03.520 line:83%
actually do not have on us
if you do all the things right.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.359 line:83%
And how to troubleshoot
most noisy areas from the past.

00:01:07.599 --> 00:01:10.439 line:83%
It's order synchronization
and fulfillment synchronization.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.159 line:85%
Let's take a look.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:16.319 line:83%
Now we are in
Business Central and let's try to

00:01:16.359 --> 00:01:19.680 line:83%
synchronize something and
see how to deal with problems.

00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:24.400 position:70% line:83%
We start with customers and I
would like to push some customers to Shopify.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.159 line:83%
I will synchronize
and oops nothing happens.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.799 line:83%
I expected at least
one customer to go there.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:31.680 line:85%
What is wrong?

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.040 line:83%
Probably the best advice or
standard advice is to explore logs.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.519 line:85%
I will go to Shopify logs.

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:41.799 line:85%
Log entries.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.120 line:85%
So many, so many.

00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:47.159 position:58% line:85%
It is so difficult to deal with them.

00:01:47.519 --> 00:01:48.079 line:85%
Not anymore.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:54.560 position:63% line:83%
So first of all, this is like how
it used to look in the previous version.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.879 line:83%
With the new upgrade, the
default view looks a bit better.

00:01:59.239 --> 00:02:05.239 position:66% line:83%
I will remove personalization, which
I made to look at as the previous version.

00:02:06.079 --> 00:02:09.439 line:83%
And now you can see
that I have additional columns.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.520 position:61% line:85%
First of all, I have columns which show

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.599 line:83%
some information
about request and response.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.080 line:85%
So at least now I can see that.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:19.000 line:83%
Here I'm trying to
create some customer data.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.080 position:77% line:83%
It will help me to distinguish
between, for example, location synchronization or

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.719 line:83%
order synchronization
or product synchronization.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.240 position:66% line:83%
The second interesting nuance is
the checkbox, which shows if this specific

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.280 position:64% line:85%
synchronization attempt had error or not.

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:38.560 line:83%
And of course, it's
more interesting to look at

00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:43.159 line:83%
the entries which
mark as entries with errors.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:49.960 position:78% line:83%
All right. So we're logging
additional information and some strange things can

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.280 line:83%
happen on either Shopify
site or on Business Central site.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:59.960 position:64% line:83%
And if we receive status code
500, something wrong was on Shopify site.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.719 line:83%
In this case, in
this case, it's better to

00:03:02.759 --> 00:03:05.280 line:83%
ask Shopify to
support through troubleshoot.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:13.639 position:72% line:83%
And to help you to talk to
Shopify support, you need to use a request ID.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.639 position:77% line:83%
It will help them to identify
specific request response dramatically faster and

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.719 position:64% line:85%
provide more detailed information to you.

00:03:21.039 --> 00:03:25.879 position:70% line:83%
So this is information which you need
to use when interacting with Shopify support.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:30.960 line:83%
But if error is 200, then
you should be with something else.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.639 line:85%
Let's explore the response.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.000 line:83%
Now many responses contain a
section which is called user error.

00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:42.080 line:83%
It means that when we
try to submit some data to

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:46.599 line:83%
Shopify as users,
something didn't work very well.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.960 position:61% line:83%
So for example, field phone
rejected content which we were sending.

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:55.120 position:61% line:85%
And it says enter a valid phone number.

00:03:55.879 --> 00:03:58.240 line:83%
So particularly
Shopify checks the phones.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.520 line:85%
And what phone do we send there?

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.599 line:83%
Yeah, it doesn't look
as a very well formatted phone.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.400 line:85%
So troubleshooting is very simple.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.080 line:83%
We will just go and
edit the phone and try again.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:16.399 line:83%
But before doing so,
let's ask ourselves a question.

00:04:17.839 --> 00:04:21.839 line:83%
If we know which errors
are bad and which records were

00:04:21.879 --> 00:04:26.279 line:83%
succeeded and which failed, do
we really need to lock all of them?

00:04:26.759 --> 00:04:28.600 line:85%
And the answer is maybe.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.439 line:83%
Let's take a look
at the Shopify shop card.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:36.519 line:83%
And you can see that
now logging mode transformed

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.959 line:83%
from the boolean on
and off into the option field.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:46.079 position:77% line:83%
Where you can of course have it
completely disabled, fully enabled or special new

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:49.560 position:64% line:85%
mode which is now default one error only.

00:04:49.959 --> 00:04:54.720 position:67% line:83%
So in this case, it will be
sending dramatically less number of errors.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.800 position:58% line:85%
Let's go back to Shopify log entries.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.240 line:85%
Delete them all just for clarity.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.959 line:85%
And activate error only mode.

00:05:10.759 --> 00:05:10.959 line:85%
Right?

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.680 line:85%
Now we will go to customers.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:18.959 line:85%
We will fix our customer.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:26.639 line:83%
Very simply, I will
just remove these values.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:35.439 position:75% line:83%
And let's go to Shopify,
customers and try to do the synchronization now.

00:05:37.079 --> 00:05:40.560 position:64% line:83%
Okay, we can see that
customer was created and what about logs?

00:05:43.959 --> 00:05:45.519 line:85%
It is empty, so it's not polluted.

00:05:45.759 --> 00:05:46.839 line:85%
It's like very good.

00:05:47.959 --> 00:05:50.920 position:64% line:83%
If you're still getting errors,
of course, they will be accumulated here.

00:05:50.959 --> 00:05:53.000 line:83%
And it makes also sense to
clean up them from time to time.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:59.680 position:70% line:83%
Not manually as I did, but you can
see that we are using retention policies now.

00:06:00.439 --> 00:06:02.680 position:64% line:85%
And we include the Shopify log entries by

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.680 line:83%
default, so they will
be cleaned up every month.

00:06:05.079 --> 00:06:08.160 position:66% line:83%
You don't need probably
entries which are more than one month old.

00:06:09.519 --> 00:06:13.319 position:70% line:83%
Also, we have the same one, but
disabled by default for Shopify data capture.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.920 line:83%
We will talk about
this feature a bit later.

00:06:17.839 --> 00:06:19.000 line:85%
All right, log is clean.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:25.839 position:72% line:83%
But some people who troubleshoot it
for some time, they already know that customer

00:06:25.879 --> 00:06:30.160 line:83%
synchronization
already provided user errors part.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:31.839 line:85%
What about other areas?

00:06:32.439 --> 00:06:34.120 line:85%
Yes, we modified queries.

00:06:34.439 --> 00:06:38.680 line:83%
Now they also, in
many cases, if not always,

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.759 line:83%
return user error
part if user error happened.

00:06:42.199 --> 00:06:44.480 line:83%
Let's take a look,
for example, to products.

00:06:44.839 --> 00:06:47.000 position:58% line:85%
And let's try to submit some product.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.560 line:85%
Home, add items.

00:06:50.879 --> 00:06:53.439 line:85%
I will be synchronizing item 118.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:56.680 line:85%
Let me pick the store and click OK.

00:06:57.279 --> 00:07:02.160 line:85%
So, 11, 18, and it failed.

00:07:03.839 --> 00:07:06.079 line:85%
Why? Let's check our log entries.

00:07:10.759 --> 00:07:11.240 line:85%
Very nice.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:12.399 line:85%
Only one entry.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.000 line:85%
And it obviously has issue.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.000 position:58% line:85%
So, let's take a look at the details.

00:07:17.639 --> 00:07:18.720 line:85%
Shopify error? No.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.160 line:85%
Something else? Yes.

00:07:20.399 --> 00:07:22.120 line:85%
Do we have user error section? Yes.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:25.079 line:85%
It complains about field SKU.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.000 line:85%
SKU can't be blank.

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:35.959 position:59% line:85%
Let's go to the shops and take a look.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.519 line:85%
Yes, SKU mapping field is empty.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.000 position:67% line:83%
Then, of course, the SKU field will be
blank when we're exporting data to Shopify.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:45.120 line:85%
But why? It is a problem right now.

00:07:45.439 --> 00:07:47.120 line:83%
So, now we are not
troubleshooting things for

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:50.240 line:83%
real, but we are
introducing the new functionality.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:56.959 position:64% line:83%
Be aware that already before
this release in one of the minor updates,

00:07:57.439 --> 00:08:02.120 position:58% line:83%
we enabled full support for
business central fulfillment service.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.680 position:64% line:83%
So, it's a separate mode how Shopify
allows you to work with external systems.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:13.240 position:56% line:83%
So, you can configure Shopify
to use on fulfillment and locations.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.240 line:85%
And in this case, it still works.

00:08:15.279 --> 00:08:17.360 line:83%
You can have
multiple of them and synchronize.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.639 position:56% line:85%
Or in Shopify, you do not care about

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.199 line:83%
locations at all
because fulfillment locations, etc.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:26.000 line:85%
will be handled on your system.

00:08:26.399 --> 00:08:28.040 line:83%
And in this case, it
will be business central.

00:08:28.959 --> 00:08:34.000 line:83%
So, now, how does
it look on Shopify side?

00:08:34.039 --> 00:08:37.639 position:64% line:85%
Let's open the Shopify admin and explore.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:43.399 position:64% line:85%
I will open some product and scroll down.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:47.720 position:72% line:83%
And you can see that in
inventory tab, you can have different options.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.159 position:61% line:85%
It allows you to choose either business

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.200 line:83%
central fulfillment
service or multiple locations.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.840 line:83%
And if you choose
business central fulfillment

00:08:55.879 --> 00:09:01.000 line:83%
service, it actually
requires you to have SKU defined.

00:09:02.039 --> 00:09:04.000 line:85%
So, SKU can't be blank.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:11.000 line:83%
So, it says exactly
here in the UI and the same

00:09:11.039 --> 00:09:13.519 line:83%
information we
received in the business central.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:14.039 line:85%
Why?

00:09:15.159 --> 00:09:17.480 line:83%
Because in the
Shopify shop locations, we have a

00:09:17.519 --> 00:09:21.399 line:83%
toggle which defines
how do we create a new product.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.200 line:83%
If you activate the toggle
on business central fulfillment,

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.519 line:83%
then new products
created on Shopify will be

00:09:27.559 --> 00:09:29.000 line:83%
assigned to business
central fulfillment locations.

00:09:29.039 --> 00:09:32.000 position:56% line:85%
And hence, they require a SKU field.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.600 line:85%
Now, back to troubleshooting area.

00:09:36.679 --> 00:09:39.480 line:83%
What do we see also
in the Shopify shop card?

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:40.519 line:85%
Something new.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:44.840 position:58% line:83%
And this is a very scary
field which is called end of support.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.600 line:83%
You should not be afraid
of it because I will explain.

00:09:49.159 --> 00:09:51.480 position:58% line:85%
Shopify also evolving pretty quickly.

00:09:51.519 --> 00:09:54.639 line:83%
So, every quarter they
release a new version of the API.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.000 line:83%
So, four times per
year, there is a new version.

00:09:57.039 --> 00:10:00.399 line:83%
And each version
is supported for one year.

00:10:01.559 --> 00:10:01.759 line:85%
Okay?

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:05.639 line:85%
So, and we try to keep up.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.600 position:56% line:83%
We always update the
recent versions or current versions.

00:10:09.879 --> 00:10:13.320 line:83%
So, it works in the
latest business central releases.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.399 line:83%
Or we also update if
necessary during minor updates.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:22.000 line:83%
So, if you upgrade in
your business central regularly,

00:10:22.039 --> 00:10:25.840 position:63% line:85%
you also receive the upgraded version of

00:10:25.879 --> 00:10:29.320 line:83%
business central
Shopify connector as well.

00:10:29.879 --> 00:10:31.679 position:58% line:85%
So, in this case, you're always good.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.120 line:83%
So, end of support
will be like a year ahead.

00:10:36.159 --> 00:10:38.919 position:59% line:85%
But we figured it out that some people

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:41.159 line:83%
stuck with the old
version of business central.

00:10:41.559 --> 00:10:44.639 line:83%
And they were using
Shopify with unsupported API.

00:10:45.159 --> 00:10:50.000 line:83%
And Shopify actually
flagged our app as having troubles.

00:10:50.039 --> 00:10:54.120 line:83%
And this information
was displayed to like everybody.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:58.879 line:83%
Not only to people who
were using old API version.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:02.759 line:83%
That's confusing
and unpleasant and creates

00:11:02.799 --> 00:11:07.600 line:83%
wrong impression for
all good upgraded customers.

00:11:08.159 --> 00:11:11.519 line:83%
So, now we have a
better information about what

00:11:11.559 --> 00:11:14.559 line:83%
will happen if you do
not upgrade in business central.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.960 line:85%
The old versions will stop working.

00:11:19.039 --> 00:11:21.799 line:85%
Just upgrade as normal.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:28.360 position:72% line:83%
Also, it makes sense to remind you
about when you're trying to do troubleshooting

00:11:28.399 --> 00:11:31.080 line:83%
about background and
foreground synchronizations.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:32.480 line:85%
Let me demonstrate.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:40.200 position:67% line:83%
If synchronization is running in the
foreground, then you don't actually see any

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:43.639 line:83%
feedback when you
execute synchronization.

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:46.519 position:56% line:85%
Like customer sync, nothing happens.

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:49.200 line:83%
You go to system create
job queue and it executes there.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.360 line:85%
And if error happens, it is there.

00:11:52.159 --> 00:11:55.080 position:56% line:85%
But if you experience some problems,

00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:00.080 line:83%
sometimes it's easier to
explore it in the foreground.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:02.679 line:85%
Let me imitate very basic problem.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:05.919 line:85%
I will just disable integration.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:10.279 position:63% line:83%
And now when I click on
seeing customers, something bad happens.

00:12:11.039 --> 00:12:14.519 position:61% line:85%
It will be in the logging system, but I

00:12:14.559 --> 00:12:16.919 line:83%
would like to catch
error in detail right away.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:20.559 line:83%
In this case, I
will disable the ground sync,

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:23.200 line:83%
which is owned by
default and try to do it again.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:28.279 position:70% line:83%
OK, in this case, I get the error and
I can copy all details, including cold stack.

00:12:28.679 --> 00:12:30.480 line:83%
Of course, in this
case, it's very primitive, but

00:12:30.519 --> 00:12:33.720 line:83%
in some scenarios, we
know it was not that simple.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:35.240 line:85%
All right.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:38.000 position:63% line:85%
Let's activate our synchronization back.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:44.360 position:88% line:83%
Another advice about
troubleshooting and connectivity, you might want to have

00:12:44.399 --> 00:12:49.559 position:72% line:83%
Shopify admin already up and running
in the same browser, probably in the same tab.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:54.799 position:72% line:83%
Then in this case, the authorization
happens smoothly and you are not redirected to

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:58.559 position:58% line:83%
a separate browser tab,
which is sometimes faster and easier.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:00.000 line:85%
All right.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:03.360 line:83%
Now let's go and
troubleshoot something business

00:13:03.399 --> 00:13:07.840 line:83%
process related, sales
orders and then fulfillments.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.840 position:61% line:85%
So how do you do order synchronization?

00:13:11.639 --> 00:13:13.080 line:85%
Let's go to the list of orders.

00:13:15.039 --> 00:13:16.759 line:85%
I have plenty of them.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:21.879 position:77% line:83%
And you can usually do, I think,
orders from Shopify, which is a standard pattern.

00:13:22.159 --> 00:13:25.559 line:83%
But what if
something doesn't work as expected

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:28.000 line:83%
or you need more
control on what is happening?

00:13:28.039 --> 00:13:31.440 line:85%
Take a look at this filter.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:33.799 line:85%
Shopify orders to import.

00:13:34.279 --> 00:13:37.480 position:59% line:85%
It's not just a filtering opportunity.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:41.159 line:85%
It is in reality the buffer table.

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:43.200 line:85%
And I will show you how to use it.

00:13:44.799 --> 00:13:46.279 line:85%
Let's create some troubles.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:51.639 line:83%
For example, let's
remove this specific order because

00:13:51.679 --> 00:13:57.000 line:83%
it is missing for some
reason and it's not in the sink.

00:13:57.039 --> 00:14:00.440 position:64% line:85%
I am trying to troubleshoot this problem.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:09.080 position:69% line:83%
I will go to the search and orders to
import, like the same as this filter string,

00:14:09.519 --> 00:14:13.159 line:83%
and it will open me
another table, another list.

00:14:13.639 --> 00:14:16.679 line:83%
And it has an action
which says get orders to import.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:24.000 position:70% line:83%
